    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "graph",
      "title": "Hypothesis tournaments, by what they produced",
      "description": "Every stage of a tournament catches and continues, so a run whose judge failed entirely still returns a ranked table \u2014 built from the prior and honestly labelled 'unrated' \u2014 that is indistinguishable from a healthy run in the logs. That is what these four states are for. `unseparated` is a legitimate and common outcome, not a fault: the leading hypotheses sat inside their own uncertainty and the run said so. `unrated` is the one to watch \u2014 it means no comparison survived, so the ordering is the prior and nothing was judged. A rising `unrated` share with `completed` falling is the gateway or the judge route failing, and no other series moves when it happens. `empty` means the screen rejected or merged everything, which points at the generator rather than the judge.",
      "datasource": "prometheus",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "span": 6,
      "fill": 0,
